/multivariable/14072974/assets/c92ab09dc71043ac3f5265202f36e38110e5e8db9f2dd115ab006721ed66d4c0.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is a type II region in the $xy$-plane:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\sqrt[3]{y}-2\\le x\\le y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$ to $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x,$ we split $D$ into two type I regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072974/assets/8ac0e7631d0baa8ba3b4c37ebe2b2b1d8efa650495d197f425aba093f342a9d3.png)\n\nNotice that the bottom and top boundaries of the left region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $y=-1\\,$ and $\\,y=(x+2)^{3}.$\n\nAlso, the bottom and top boundaries of the right region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $y=x\\,$ and $\\,y=1.$\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-3\\le x\\le -1,\\,-1\\le y\\le (x+2)^{3}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,x\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}{\\int }_{-1}^{(x+2)^{3}}{\\int }_{y/2}^{x+4}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{x}^{1}{\\int }_{y/2}^{x+4}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377689 13194139535977 true] [17592186377688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377690 13194139535977 true] [17592186377688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377691 13194139535977 true] [17592186377688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377692 13194139535977 true] [17592186377688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377693 13194139535977 true] [17592186377688 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535977 true] [17592186377688 1041 "selection" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377688 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377693 13194139535977 true] [17592186377688 1110 #uuid "1661af9e-d602-5459-9e37-c8d1bdef06b6" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377689 1034 "p=-2,\\,\\,\\,q=\\sqrt[3]{x+2},\\,\\,\\,r=-x" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377689 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377689 1111 #uuid "8168ba34-d7c2-549b-8c10-a1d3d2f5b62d" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377690 1034 "p=-1,\\,\\,\\,q=(x+2)^{3},\\,\\,\\,r={x}^{2}" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377690 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377690 1111 #uuid "8b95ba1a-490c-5097-affb-874efe154a61" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377691 1034 "p=-1,\\,\\,\\,q=\\sqrt[3]{x+2},\\,\\,\\,r=x" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377691 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377691 1111 #uuid "d6a5f30b-9aba-50cd-a015-55f1c1c1548d" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377692 1034 "p=-2,\\,\\,\\,q=3(x+2),\\,\\,\\,r=-x" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377692 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377692 1111 #uuid "53062854-819e-5797-a8ea-2a39303974a4" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377693 1034 "p=-1,\\,\\,\\,q=(x+2)^{3},\\,\\,\\,r=x" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377693 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377693 1111 #uuid "e56a5336-c4aa-5c21-a1d1-a08776f3d140" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377694 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377695 13194139535977 true] [17592186377694 1089 "q-162376" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377694 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535977 true] [17592186377694 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072974/assets/c72489a2d33a181fe7bc07d5cc017b93daccac51889cbb61edd64d4ee34429df.png)\n\nThe triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over the region $R$ (shown above) can be expressed as the following repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}+1}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nRewrite this repeated integral by integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $y,$ and then $x.$" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377694 1113 #uuid "7b94d854-420e-5d57-988d-2367c6e7514b" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377694 1145 "From the given repeated integral, we see that $R$ can be written as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}},\\,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}+1}\n$$\n\nWe wish to rewrite our triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,y)}^{{u}_{2}(x,y)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nSince both repeated integrals first integrate with respect to $z,$ the $z$-limits remain the same as before:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}+1}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072974/assets/98aa4c0a436e4649ccd3d48a53fbf94b0341bf30b95745c4d052381680d223cf.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is a type II region in the $xy$-plane:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$ to $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x,$ we write $D$ as a type I region.\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is \n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,y=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nThen, the type I representation of the region $D$ is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072974/assets/47380c108c5b271761de2a027399bbd5981f2a9bdff21e498d73d0b430d070c7.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}+1}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377696 13194139535977 true] [17592186377695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377697 13194139535977 true] [17592186377695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377698 13194139535977 true] [17592186377695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377699 13194139535977 true] [17592186377695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377700 13194139535977 true] [17592186377695 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535977 true] [17592186377695 1041 "selection" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377695 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377698 13194139535977 true] [17592186377695 1110 #uuid "ea5a9e7d-d0f8-5005-b714-79691a97451c" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377696 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}+1}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377696 1111 #uuid "e85a6647-6a17-5de0-a1b6-ab16b8282c22" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377697 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377697 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377697 1111 #uuid "80d7d9a1-4e52-5904-8b11-18df21911037" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377698 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}+1}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377698 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377698 1111 #uuid "3a02f5fa-98ce-51ad-a008-c114c99b3a2a" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377699 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377699 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 131941