\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072974/assets/a89646433c8851f66c94092b75fae7b46b01f31c69ca03d338464b87bd7f5df4.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is a type II region in the $xy$-plane:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le y}\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$ to $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x,$ we write $D$ as a type I region.\n\nNotice that the bottom boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is \n\n$$\nx=y\\,⟹\\,y=x\n$$\n\nand the top boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=1.\n$$\n\nThen, the type I representation of the region $D$ is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,x\\le y\\le 1},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072974/assets/1604e44050208cfb3b4dd81d35bff9769c7498d8304583d5ba92ad4b2f62fd05.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377703 13194139535977 true] [17592186377702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377704 13194139535977 true] [17592186377702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377705 13194139535977 true] [17592186377702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377706 13194139535977 true] [17592186377702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377707 13194139535977 true] [17592186377702 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535977 true] [17592186377702 1041 "selection" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377702 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377705 13194139535977 true] [17592186377702 1110 #uuid "6631bb4a-11be-5954-8d9b-b5ec3051ef6f" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377703 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377703 1111 #uuid "6cb2015a-3b46-5e6b-904c-1d38c1310142" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377704 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377704 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377704 1111 #uuid "2fdd0468-c58a-5b5e-b04a-97e7ba719976" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377705 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377705 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377705 1111 #uuid "2076f531-0026-5c23-9b9b-c9daa53f5341" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377706 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377706 1111 #uuid "1af92249-c4df-50ef-bdd6-973c66f689a9" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377707 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377707 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377707 1111 #uuid "540c103a-e9e9-5635-a3bf-d504994454e2" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377708 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377709 13194139535977 true] [17592186377708 1089 "q-162406" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377708 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535977 true] [17592186377708 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072974/assets/fcc776a63cd1ac9fc5ec91157652ce9e75c6ee515eca8c6223309521cc300b61.png)\n\nThe triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over the region $R$ (shown above) can be expressed as the following repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-4/x}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{2+xy/2}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nRewrite this repeated integral by integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y.$" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377708 1113 #uuid "b7fcce9c-e434-56cb-96bb-7fe09af48258" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377708 1145 "From the given repeated integral, we see that $R$ can be written as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\,-\\frac{4}{x}\\le y\\le -1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2+\\frac{xy}{2}}\n$$\n\nWe wish to rewrite our triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(y)}^{{v}_{2}(y)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,y)}^{{u}_{2}(x,y)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nSince both repeated integrals first integrate with respect to $z,$ the $z$-limits remain the same as before:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(y)}^{{v}_{2}(y)}{\\int }_{0}^{2+xy/2}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072974/assets/1f30c28c7c048faae864da08a5a6d67d0c6346b27c00a9e7726234531f2f0783.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is a type I region in the $xy$-plane:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\,-\\frac{4}{x}\\le y\\le -1}\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$ to $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y,$ we write $D$ as a type II region.\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{4}{x}\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{4}{y}\n$$\n\nand the left boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=1.\n$$\n\nThen, the type II representation of the region $D$ is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-4\\le y\\le -1,\\,\\,1\\le x\\le -\\frac{4}{y}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072974/assets/acc210f36bccb873526172149b85941bd42bc1648a464862562723fedca27bcb.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{-4}^{-1}{\\int }_{1}^{-4/y}{\\int }_{0}^{2+xy/2}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377710 13194139535977 true] [17592186377709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377711 13194139535977 true] [17592186377709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377712 13194139535977 true] [17592186377709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377713 13194139535977 true] [17592186377709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377714 13194139535977 true] [17592186377709 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535977 true] [17592186377709 1041 "selection" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377709 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377711 13194139535977 true] [17592186377709 1110 #uuid "e1043adb-69e6-5331-aeab-f995c028b8b9" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377710 1034 "{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}{\\int }_{1}^{-4/y}{\\int }_{0}^{4/(xy)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377710 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377710 1111 #uuid "f7ae675e-4ed8-571c-91e3-6f972fd96c1a" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377711 1034 "{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}{\\int }_{1}^{-4/y}{\\int }_{0}^{2+xy/2}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377711 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377711 1111 #uuid "c73526c2-ee4f-58f7-b19f-608dc444f564" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377712 1034 "{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}{\\int }_{-4/y}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4/(xy)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377712 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535977 true] [17592186377712 1111 #uuid "3beb4534-bb8c-50b1-b430-50c8aa3256ca" 13194139535977 true] [17592186377713 1034 "{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{-4/y}{\\int }_{0}^{2+xy/2}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\